.TH CJSON_BOOL_VAL 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cjson_bool_val, cjson_int_val, cjson_double_val, cjson_str_val \- read a scalar value from a DOM node
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cjson.h>

bool        cjson_bool_val(cjson node);
long long   cjson_int_val(cjson node);
double      cjson_double_val(cjson node);
const char *cjson_str_val(cjson node);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Each function returns the value stored in node, asserting via fatal_err()
if the node's type does not match.

cjson_str_val() returns a pointer to the node's own internal copy of
the string; the caller must not free it.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cjson_type (3)
